# /etc/w2c/w2c.env — the PLATFORM's half of this box's environment: where its state is, who this server is, its
# secrets. Every unit reads it, and `vms.env` (the VMS subsystems' settings) after it. /etc/w2c is a LINK to
# /data/platform/etc (`install-obsd.sh` lays it): on the data partition, never in a rootfs slot (М9 Lesson 5) — an
# OS update must not change which store this box is a member of.
# ================================================================================================
# NOTES — what every part of this file does and why (kept beside the code, not in a separate document)
# ================================================================================================
# # w2c.env.example — `/etc/w2c/w2c.env`: the platform's settings, the half every unit reads first
#
# **Role.** The platform is w2c, the VMS is one of its subsystems (the product's rule, 3 October): what a process
# needs to be a member of the platform — its store, its events archive, its server's name, its labels, its key —
# is here, in one file that does not change when a subsystem is added; what a VMS process needs to do its work —
# capacity, the media directory, its own volume, the backfill window — is in `vms.env`. Every Quadlet unit names
# both, `EnvironmentFile=/etc/w2c/w2c.env` then `EnvironmentFile=/etc/vms/vms.env` (a name set in both: the second
# wins) — the product's pair and paths. The FILES live on the data partition, for the reason above: /etc/w2c is a
# link to /data/platform/etc, /etc/vms to /data/vms/etc (the owner's decision: on an A/B box /etc is on the slot an
# update replaces), and a unit says /etc/…, never the target. `tests/test_deploy_units.py` checks that every unit
# reads the two and that each variable is in its own half.
#
# - `PLATFORM_DIR` — ALL the platform's mutable state under one directory (`w2cplatform.runtime.DATA`): `<dir>/config`
#   (FileVariables — rows, assignments, placement, epochs, slots, idempotency keys) and `<dir>/objects`
#   (FsObjectStore — heartbeats, the snapshot), both setgid `w2c-store`; `<dir>/events`, the events archive; in a
#   cluster `<dir>/configstore`. Its `etc/` is this file's home. Every unit mounts the two stores at the same paths —
#   never the whole directory, whose `etc/secrets` holds the key ring. In М11 the rows move to `configstore`.
# - `ARCHIVE` — the platform's events archive, the resource's tree (`runtime.events_root`; unset:
#   `$PLATFORM_DIR/events`). A key of THIS file since the archive is the platform's (the owner, 4 October): the
#   resource owns it and runs as `w2c`, every process that writes buckets is a client of the group `w2c-events`.
# - `PLATFORM_STORE` — the config store, said as a URL and nothing else (`w2cplatform.variables.store_url`; its old
#   name `CONFIG_URL` is still read). Unset: the files under `$PLATFORM_DIR/config`, in-process — on one box there
#   is no daemon, no hop and no second quorum. In a cluster: `configstore:///run/configstore/<role>.sock`.
# - What a RUNTIME hands every process by name, so that none of them learns which runtime it was
#   (`w2cplatform/runtime.py`): `SERVER_NAME` (whose resource this process writes into; unset: the hostname),
#   `LABELS` (what this server can reach, comma-separated; unset: none), `BOX_ID` (this machine's id, the host part
#   of a recorder's hold). Quadlet sets `WORKER_NAME=%i` per unit and nothing else — on one box the hostname is the
#   server and there are no labels, so the three are commented out below.
# - Secrets: the cluster's key ring is a FILE, `/etc/w2c/secrets/platform.key` (`python3 -m w2cplatform.sealing new`;
#   0640, group `w2c-secrets`), never a value here — this file is read by every unit, the key goes only into the
#   three that open sealed fields (the console, the holder, the recorder), mounted at `/run/secrets/platform.key`
#   with `SECRETS_KEY` set in each of those units, which join `w2c-secrets`.
# - The spares' script (`w2c-spares.sh`, a platform script run by `w2c-spares*.timer`) reads this file too:
#   `CONSOLE` and the ceilings per role.
# ================================================================================================
PLATFORM_DIR=/data/platform
ARCHIVE=/data/platform/events
# PLATFORM_STORE=file:///data/platform/config
# SERVER_NAME=
# LABELS=
# BOX_ID=
# the spares' script: where the console answers, and how many spares of each role this server may run
# CONSOLE=http://127.0.0.1:8080
# MAX_RECORDERS=8
# MAX_WORKERS=4
# MAX_GATEWAYS=4
# MAX_EVALUATORS=4
